Package: biasratio
Title: Bias Fraction and Bias-Effect Ratio: Quantifying Residual Systematic Bias in Observational Studies
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zhechun", "Zeng", , "zengzhechun@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: Quantifies residual systematic bias in observational effect
    estimates using negative control outcomes. Building on the OHDSI empirical
    calibration framework ('EmpiricalCalibration'), the bias fraction (BF)
    expresses the share of the total calibrated signal (bias plus residual
    effect) attributable to systematic bias on a bounded 0-1 scale, and the
    bias-effect ratio (BER) expresses the same information as an unbounded
    ratio (BF = BER / (1 + BER)). Each estimate is classified as
    bias-dominated, mixed, or effect-dominated. Provides log-scale (and
    logit-scale) bootstrap confidence intervals with bootstrap-median point
    estimates, a Fieller confidence set for the underlying ratio,
    leave-one-out sensitivity analysis, negative control diagnostics, and
    'ggplot2' visualizations designed for clinical audiences.
